<title>USA: Baldwin &amp; Lyons chairman Aldin dies.</title>
<headline>Baldwin &amp; Lyons chairman Aldin dies.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS, Ind. 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Baldwin &amp; Lyons Inc said Monday that John Aldin, its chairman and chief executive officer, has died. He was 64.</p>
<p>Prior to becoming chairman in 1984, Aldin was president and chief executive of Indiana Insurance Co. Aldin founded Indianapolis-based Hoosier Insurance Co, a subsidiary of Baldwin &amp; Lyons, and served as its chairman until its sale in 1995.</p>
<p>Other details were not immediately available.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
